2186571648 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572072 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "b9df1b13-c754-54c2-9e96-913d5093b7bf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572076 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186571711 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572076 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186571741 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572076 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186571828 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572076 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186571842 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572076 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186571894 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572076 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572076 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572076 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186571842 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572076 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "c506eaa0-7955-591f-814f-18652414f794" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572099 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186571574 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572099 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186571592 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572099 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186571675 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572099 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186571881 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572099 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186571955 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572099 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572099 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572099 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186571675 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572099 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f5de6842-82de-5750-82ca-c06c56c35e1a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572133 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186572069 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572133 #edb/ref 1069 "q-67426" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572133 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572133 #edb/ref 1071 "Solve the equation $\\frac{6}{x-5}=\\frac{2}{x}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572133 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "50efbd3d-db78-53ec-922c-e4529ac97e50" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572133 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we note that\n\n- $x=5$ cannot be a solution since this would make the denominator on the left-hand side zero\n\n- $x=0$ cannot be a solution since this would make the denominator on the right-hand side zero\n\nWe can flip an equation involving two fractions as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{a}{b}=\\frac{c}{d}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{b}{a}=\\frac{d}{c}\n$$\n\nThe above technique works whenever $a$ and $c$ are both different from zero.\n\nTherefore, we can flip the given equation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-5}{6}=\\frac{x}{2}\n$$\n\nNext, we write both fractions using the least common denominator $6.$ The above equation becomes\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-5}{6}=\\frac{3x}{6}\n$$\n\nWe can now solve this equation with the addition and the multiplication principles:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6\\cdot \\frac{x-5}{6} & =6\\cdot \\frac{3x}{6} \\\\ x-5 & =3x \\\\ x-x-5 & =3x-x \\\\ -5 & =2x \\\\ (\\frac{1}{2})\\cdot (-5) & =(\\frac{1}{2})\\cdot (2x) \\\\ -\\frac{5}{2} & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that the solution is $x=-\\frac{5}{2}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572135 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186572001 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572135 #edb/ref 1069 "q-118542" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572135 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572135 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/b6/b604de78802c70f2fa5960de7560b6adde1b4e72153aa92e22411507ef70320f.png)\n\nThe vectors $\\text{a}$ and $\\text{b}$ are shown in the diagram above. Which of the following could be $-a+b?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572135 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "59df03f5-b0de-547f-a369-251d1939cc3e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572135 #edb/ref 1074 "We interpret  $-a+b$ as the addition\n\n$$\n(-a)+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $-a$ is the vector that has the same magnitude as $a$ but goes in the direction *opposite* of $a.$\n\nFinally, we use the triangle law to add the vectors $-a$ and $b:$ \n\n- We can start $-a$ from an arbitrary point on the plane.\n\n- Next, we draw the vector that is equal to $b$ and has its tail placed at the head of $-a.$\n\n- Now, according to the triangle law of addition, the resultant is the vector that goes from the tail of $-\\text{a}$ to the head of $\\text{b}$, as shown below.\n\n![](images/7e/7ed9a5ed605856d8c81976951711a3a5d2561ca1874843e8a618972151acf3c2.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572136 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186572044 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572136 #edb/ref 1069 "q-111297" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572136 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572136 #edb/ref 1071 "$(z-7)(z+5)=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572136 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5fbbc181-ab02-53e1-a097-fa8b9ef68cb3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572136 #edb/ref 1074 "We take each term of the first binomial and multiply it by the second binomial. Then, we simplify by collecting like terms.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(z-7)(z+5) & = \\\\ z(z+5)+(-7)(z+5) & = \\\\ {z}^{2}+5z-7z-35 & = \\\\ {z}^{2}-2z-35\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572169 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186572016 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572169 #edb/ref 1069 "q-34204" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572169 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572169 #edb/ref 1071 "Simplify $-2\\sqrt[3]{xy}-4\\sqrt{xy}+6\\sqrt{xy}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572169 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b56a30ba-e6cb-544a-bbd5-8a6dcd830acc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572169 #edb/ref 1074 "We can combine the two $\\sqrt{xy}$ terms together, but we cannot combine $\\sqrt{xy}$ and $\\sqrt[3]{xy}$ term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2\\sqrt[3]{xy}-4\\sqrt{xy}+6\\sqrt{xy} & = \\\\ -2\\sqrt[3]{xy}+(-4+6)\\sqrt{xy} & = \\\\ -2\\sqrt[3]{xy}+2\\sqrt{xy} & \\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572170 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186572099 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572170 #edb/ref 1069 "q-73877" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572170 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572170 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following number lines gives the solution to $-1<\\frac{5x+7}{3}\\le 4?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572170 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b6a1d8df-14fd-58d7-a188-333aa892620d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572170 #edb/ref 1074 "We isolate $x$ by applying the addition and multiplication principles, as usual.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & <\\frac{5x+7}{3}\\le 4 \\\\ -1\\cdot 3 & <\\frac{5x+7}{3}\\cdot 3\\le 4\\cdot 3 \\\\ -3 & <5x+7\\le 12 \\\\ -3-7 & <5x+7-7\\le 12-7 \\\\ -10 & <5x\\le 5 \\\\ \\frac{-10}{5} & <\\frac{5x}{5}\\le \\frac{5}{5} \\\\ -2 & <x\\le 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can represent this solution using a number line, as follows.\n\n![](images/a7/a70249a33b29eeec3c36c1077486fecfcdf19eb653973d41d19987be4a80be0a.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572177 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186572048 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572177 #edb/ref 1069 "q-52934" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572177 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572177 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/76/766f2cc9fe5a205c4eadfa50c6ba87145106efd97db51041aea4629313a8d80f.png)\n\nFind $m∠N$ in the quadrilateral $OMNP$ above." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572177 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c85d6d2c-7d60-53c2-9293-99f57c859bc7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572177 #edb/ref 1074 "A quadrilateral has $n=4$ sides. Therefore, the sum of the interior angles of a quadrilateral must be \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{180}^{∘}\\cdot (n-2) & ={180}^{∘}\\cdot (4-2) \\\\  & ={180}^{∘}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & ={360}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding up the internal angles and solving for $m∠N,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠O+m∠M+m∠N+m∠P & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ {60}^{∘}+{40}^{∘}+m∠N+{40}^{∘} & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ {140}^{∘}+m∠N & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ m∠N & ={220}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572182 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186572036 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572182 #edb/ref 1069 "q-21137" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572182 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572182 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/f5/f58bf69e5449710785053d04ccec129bd6ed51c67b29ad8701c0b66e842897c0.png)\n\nWhat element of the circle is depicted in the diagram above?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572182 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d2ee3b0e-faf8-58c6-aa1f-4a103b69243b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572182 #edb/ref 1074 "The region shown in the diagram is bounded by the arc $\\overset{⌢}{AB}$ of the circle and the radii $\\overset{―}{OA}$ and $\\overset{―}{OB}.$ So, this region represents the circular sector $OAB.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572189 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186572062 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572189 #edb/ref 1069 "q-222327" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572189 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572189 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/d8/d87a618227b9f71d205080ca18321b988c0aae321ac382ace14ba3c42cb640a5.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the image of the graph $y=|x|$ under the action of a single translation. What is the equation of this curve?\n\nThe equation of this curve is $y=$\n{{field-1}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572189 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "df7c4c47-80d6-5201-b456-75a42c3c1fbc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572189 #edb/ref 1074 "Remember that $y=|x|+a$ is a vertical translation of the absolute value graph $y=|x|$ by $a$ units up.\n\nHere, the graph is moved up by $6$ units. This corresponds to $a=6.$ \n\nTherefore, the equation of the curve is $y=|x|+6.$\n\n![](images/91/9175449249193509c2cfd0717004516d51f15811391d3e056d552166df6da8b1.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572195 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186572033 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572195 #edb/ref 1069 "q-237175" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572195 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572195 #edb/ref 1071 "The kinetic energy $K$ of a non-rotating object, measured in joules ($\\text{J}$), varies directly with the **square** of the object velocity $v,$ measured in meters per second ($\\text{m/s}$). If $K=100\\,\\text{J}$ when the velocity is $v=5\\,\\text{m/s},$ then what is the constant of variation? You do not need to state the units.\n\nThe constant of variation is\n{{field-1}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572195 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "eb47fc03-5b60-58b0-9d3f-f700dc615259" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572195 #edb/ref 1074 "The kinetic energy $K$ is directly proportional to the square of the velocity $v.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nK=k{v}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $k$ is the constant of variation.\n\nWe are told that $K=100\\,\\text{J}$ when $v=5\\,\\text{m/s}.$ We can use this information to solve for $k,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}100 & =k\\cdot {5}^{2} \\\\ 100 & =k\\cdot 25 \\\\ \\frac{100}{25} & =k \\\\ 4 & =k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the constant of variation is $4.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572197 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186572059 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572197 #edb/ref 1069 "q-147067" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572197 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572197 #edb/ref 1071 "Jane writes down a $28$ digit number, where $\\frac{3}{7}$ of the digits are odd. How many even digits are in the number?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572197 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f004f03a-3145-589b-b783-dc999853f011" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572197 #edb/ref 1074 "We are given that the ratio of odd digits to the total number of digits is $\\frac{3}{7}.$ \n\nIn this fraction, the numerator represents the number of odd digits, and the denominator represents the total number of digits.\n\nWe can make a denominator of $28$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $4:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{3\\times 4}{7\\times 4}=\\frac{12}{28}\n$$\n\nTherefore, there are $12$ odd digits in the number. \nSo, the number of even digits is\n\n$$\n28-12=16.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572207 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186572258 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572207 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "124de9ee-a94e-5929-b297-9e1dae572494" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572207 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186572170 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572215 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "28439026-9df7-5022-8efd-98cccd4a8a55" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572215 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186572191 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572217 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186572259 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572217 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "2d27af44-6643-544f-a9d1-40b69565d526" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572217 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186572169 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572219 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186572266 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572219 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "3048f141-ef5f-5cad-b832-c238b4127174" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572219 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186572182 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572233 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186572260 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572233 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "5c92526c-7bd1-56e0-8aa4-18d50af53467" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572233 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186489211 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572250 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186572262 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572250 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "8f7aa20f-720c-53d1-8564-0adb00dacfcd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572250 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186572197 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572258 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186572250 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572258 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a84c9e26-077d-569b-a6fb-1f5c8eb64083" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572258 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186572195 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572259 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186572207 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572259 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a91d9636-d4ea-5123-88a8-d4776fc22411" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572259 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186115865 #e